<title>USA: Silver Diner Q1 April 20 net loss widens.</title>
<headline>Silver Diner Q1 April 20 net loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>ROCKVILLE, Md. 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sixteen Weeks Ended</p>
<p>							Apr 20,     Apr 21,</p>
<p>							   1997	 1996</p>
<p> Net sales				     $6,132,204  $4,894,428</p>
<p> Interest expense					--     174,709</p>
<p> Investment income			    (114,165)    (33,102)</p>
<p>   NET LOSS				     (748,062)   (698,091)</p>
<p> Net loss per common share		     (0.06)	(0.11)</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares outstanding</p>
<p>						   11,575,266   6,186,505</p>
<p>NOTE:  Silver Diner Inc said its net loss per share decreased from $0.11 in first quarter 1996 to $0.06 in first quarter 1997 due to an increase in the weighted average number of average shares outstanding-from approximately 6.2 million shares to 11.6 million shares-as a result of the merger with Food Trends Acquisition Corp in March 1996 and a private equity placement in July 1996.</p>
</text>
